T:Going to the Well for Water
T:the Kaiser
C:John T. Blair (1957)
L:1/8
M:9/8
N:TROTTING TO LARNE. Irish, Slip Jig. A Major. Composed by John T. Blair in
N:1957. Ossian OSS 84, Boys of the Lough - "The Open Road." Sarah Bauhan.
N:Paul de Grae notes:
N:AKA "Going to the Well for Water" (also the name of another slide) or "The Kaiser",
N:pronounced "kaysher", the nickname of a local character in Sliabh Luachra.
N:Originally in A, transposed by John Skelton, who got the tune from Cathal McConnell
